        "text": {
            "description_html": "<b>Fusion AR-Z2, Elite Collection Virginia Lever with Cambridge Rose</b>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nThe Virginia Lever with Cambridge Rose is available in 5 finishes including brushed nickel and oil rubbed bronze--all of which bring out the traditional styling of the leverset. As a wave type lever, the classic shape brings a sense of movement to a room. The Virginia Leverset will fit 1-3/8 inch to 2 inch thick doors and has an adjustable backset for either 2-3/8 inches or 2-3/4 inches; and since it is part of Fusion's Elite Collection, it has concealed screw mounting for a polished look once installed.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>Features</b> of the Fusion AR-Z2 Traditional Virginia Leverset with Cambridge Rose:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Solid Brass/Bronze Construction</li>\r\n<li>Cycle Tested to ANSI Standards</li>\r\n<li>Exclusive Fusion lever spring assembly for lifetime performance.</li>\r\n<li>Reversible Latchbolt in matching/coordinating finish.</li>\r\n<li>Easy assembly with alignment block and rose posts.</li>\r\n<li>Concealed screw rose cover.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>Specifications</b> for the Virginia Leverset:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Lever Length: 4-1/5\"</li>\r\n<li>Projection: 2-3/5\"</li>\r\n<li>Rose Diameter: 2-5/8\"</li>\r\n<li>Door Thickness: adjustable for 1-3/8\" to 2\"</li>\r\n<li>Backset: adjustable for 2-3/8\" to 2-3/4\"</li>\r\n<li>Material: Solid Brass and Bronze</li>\r\n<li>Standard Latch Rotation is 40 Degrees.</li>\r\n<li>Square corner latches and strike plates.</li>\r\n<li>Lifetime Limited Warranty on workmanship, materials, and operation.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>When Selecting a Function:</b>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><b>Single Dummy:</b> Non-functional pull to match trim on one side of the door. Just for looks, it does not latch and does not lock.</li>\r\n<li><b>Dummy Set:</b> Non-functional pull to match trim on both sides of the door. Just for looks, it does not latch and does not lock.</li>\r\n<li><b>Passage (Hall or Closet):</b> For doors that don't need locking.</li>\r\n<li><b>Privacy (Bedroom or Bathroom):</b> For doors that could need locking.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>Note: The Single Dummy Function is Handed</b>. All other functions are non-handed. <a href=\"/pages/how-to-order-door-hardware\"><b>Handing Guide</b></a>\r\n</p>",
